93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (The major form of current communication is wireless networks \(IEEE 802.11\), yet because their signals are broadcast freely over the air, they are inherently unsafe. Unencrypted management frames are a serious vulnerability that may be readily exploited by attackers using tools like Python's Scapy to track devices or execute Deauthentication DoS attacks.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (The Wireless Intrusion Detection and Monitoring System \(WIDMS\) was created as a real-time detection tool to mitigate these hazards. Built using Kali Linux, Python, and Wireshark, WIDMS enables users to visualize anomalies, log suspicious events, and receive alerts before significant damage occurs. The project functions as an instructional platform that connects theoretical security principles with proactive, practical implementation by fusing attack simulation with defensive monitoring.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
