179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The Wireless Intrusion Detection and Monitoring System \(WIDMS\) successfully demonstrated Layer-2 security risks in IEEE 802.11 networks by leveraging Kali Linux, Python Scapy, and Wireshark to detect deauthentication floods, probe tracking, and hidden SSID exploits. While currently constrained to a controlled lab environment for threat detection, the project provides a vital educational foundation regarding vulnerable unencrypted management frames. It underscores the power of open-source security monitoring, paving the way for future enhancements such as automated machine learning anomaly detection and active mitigation via Protected Management Frames \(802.11w\).)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
